I am sitting in the S-Bahn.
I am riding home.
I look out of the window.
I see the streets and buildings.
I see the city map in my head.
I think about the man with the dog.
He is very friendly.
Now I understand the city much better.
My part of Berlin is not unfamiliar anymore.
I know the way to the centre now.
And I know the way home.
The S-Bahn stops.
That is my stop.
I get off.
I walk to my flat.
I am tired, but happy.
